ent-BaseWeaponPistol = BasePistol
    .desc = A rooty tooty point and shooty.
ent-BaseWeaponRevolver = BaseWeaponRevolver
    .desc = A rooty tooty point and shooty.
ent-WeaponPistolAPS = stechkin APS
    .desc = A high quality firearm issued to SNKVD elites and high ranking officials. It's half pistol, half closing argument. Uses .40 ammo.
ent-WeaponPistolBlueguard = sp-8t
    .desc = A pistol that packs a punch for brig defense, just as NanoTrasen intended.
ent-WeaponPistolCobra = cobra
    .desc = Integrally suppressed semi-automatic pistol used by the Syndicate, firing caseless subsonic rounds. Favored by any agent who likes to keep things quiet and leave no evidence behind. Feeds from .25 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolCobraWorn = cobra
    .desc = Integrally suppressed semi-automatic pistol used by the Syndicate, firing caseless subsonic rounds. Favored by any agent who likes to keep things quiet and leave no evidence behind. Feeds from .25 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = Second Hand
ent-WeaponPistolColdCase = cold maletín
    .desc = An antiquated design of a pistol, truly a stylish choice.
ent-WeaponPistolDP = due process
    .desc = A pistol that packs a punch for brig defense, just as NanoTrasen intended.
ent-WeaponPistolDeagle = jungle hawk
    .desc = A high-caliber handgun designed for putting down large game.
ent-WeaponPistolEchis = echis
    .desc = A cyborg-mounted weapon system based on the Viper pistol. Creates ammunition on the fly from an internal fabricator, which slowly self-charges.
ent-WeaponPistolEnforcer = enforcer
    .desc = A versatile pistol of modern design.
ent-WeaponPistolForged = forged pistola
    .desc = A reliable magazine-fed pistol made by the best tider blacksmiths.
ent-WeaponPistolGoldenMk58 = golden mk 58
    .desc = An expensive and rare golden variant of the Mk58, only given out to the elite. Doesn't actually have any functional differences, though. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolGoldenMk58HighCapacity = golden mk 58
    .desc = An expensive and rare golden variant of the Mk58, only given out to the elite. Doesn't actually have any functional differences, though. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = 16 rounds
ent-WeaponPistolImprovised = improvised pistola
    .desc = A cobbled together pistol with an internal magazine. More reliable, but still liable to blow up in your face.
ent-WeaponPistolM1911 = m1911
    .desc = A classic .45 handgun with a small magazine capacity.
ent-WeaponPistolMakarov = makarov
    .desc = A cheap and cumbersome pistol, with a dot on the rear sight indicating the direction in which it tends to misfire, as this model does not shoot straight. Uses .35 auto ammo.
ent-WeaponPistolMakeshiftCrafted = makeshift pistola
    .desc = Little more than a space eoka. Very unreliable.
ent-WeaponPistolMk58 = mk 58
    .desc = Designed by NanoTrasen’s Small Arms Division, the Mk58 is a conventional semi-automatic pistol with a simple recoil-operated action and excellent reliability. The standard sidearm of NanoTrasen’s station security and emergency response teams. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolMk58HighCapacity = mk 58
    .desc = Designed by NanoTrasen’s Small Arms Division, the Mk58 is a conventional semi-automatic pistol with a simple recoil-operated action and excellent reliability. The standard sidearm of NanoTrasen’s station security and emergency response teams. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = 16 rounds
ent-WeaponPistolMk58Nonlethal = mk 58
    .desc = Designed by NanoTrasen’s Small Arms Division, the Mk58 is a conventional semi-automatic pistol with a simple recoil-operated action and excellent reliability. The standard sidearm of NanoTrasen’s station security and emergency response teams. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = Non-lethal
ent-WeaponPistolN1984 = N1984
    .desc = An exceptionally powerful ‘hand cannon’ designed as part of NanoTrasen's BFG initiative. Chambered in .45, the lord’s caliber, it is generally considered too unwieldy for standard use but has become something of a status symbol among NanoTrasen officials. Feeds from .45 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolN1984Nonlethal = N1984
    .desc = An exceptionally powerful ‘hand cannon’ designed as part of NanoTrasen's BFG initiative. Chambered in .45, the lord’s caliber, it is generally considered too unwieldy for standard use but has become something of a status symbol among NanoTrasen officials. Feeds from .45 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = Non-lethal
ent-WeaponPistolSP8AR = sp-8ar
    .desc = A pistol that packs a punch for brig defense, just as NanoTrasen intended.
ent-WeaponPistolStechkin = stechkin pistola
    .desc = A small, easily concealable .40 handgun. Has a threaded barrel for suppressors. Uses .40 ammo.
ent-WeaponPistolTSFBorg = TSF-Model17
    .desc = A cyborg-mounted weapon system based on the Model 17 pistol. Creates ammunition on the fly from an internal fabricator, which slowly self-charges.
    .suffix = Cyborg
ent-WeaponPistolTSFModel17 = TSF-Model17
    .desc = A standard-issue sidearm of the Trans Solar Federation, the Model 17 serves TSF peacekeepers across the galaxy. Built with proven reliability and chambered in .35 auto, this pistol remains a trusted tool of law enforcement. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolViper = viper
    .desc = A common handgun illegally modified by the Syndicate. The Viper sports a selector switch between semi-auto, "rock and roll", and "spray and pray". The standard sidearm for any soldier who fights under the three serpents. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
ent-WeaponPistolViperWorn = viper
    .desc = A common handgun illegally modified by the Syndicate. The Viper sports a selector switch between semi-auto, "rock and roll", and "spray and pray". The standard sidearm for any soldier who fights under the three serpents. Feeds from .35 pistol magazines.
    .suffix = Second Hand
ent-WeaponRevolverDeckard = deckard
    .desc = A beautifully machined, custom-built revolver. Used when there is no time for the Voight-Kampff test. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum.
ent-WeaponRevolverDispatcher = dispatcher
    .desc = The NT Model 7 Service Revolver, known unofficially as the 'Dispatcher.' chambered in .45 Magnum with robust stopping power for putting an end to any non-compliance. A true timeless classic carried amongst NanoTrasen's elite security staff.
ent-WeaponRevolverForged = forged revólver
    .desc = The best Tider engineering can offer, a revolver with the ability to hold 4 bullets!
ent-WeaponRevolverImprovised = improvised revólver
    .desc = A revolver that has two barrels and no cylinder. Can you really call this a revolver?
ent-WeaponRevolverInspector = inspector
    .desc = A double-action revolver manufactured by various companies. It is readily available on the civilian market, making it a popular choice among private investigators. You feel lucky just holding it. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum.
ent-WeaponRevolverMakeshift = makeshift revólver
    .desc = Little more than a hand-cannon with a high chance of blowing up in your face.
ent-WeaponRevolverMateba = mateba
    .desc = A modern revolver used by NanoTrasen’s elite, near mythical ‘Death Squad’ task force. Its unique trigger action and barrel placement enable a high fire rate with minimal muzzle flip. Many have looked down this barrel, but few have lived to tell of it. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum.
ent-WeaponRevolverMatebaAP = mateba
    .desc = A modern revolver used by NanoTrasen’s elite, near mythical ‘Death Squad’ task force. Its unique trigger action and barrel placement enable a high fire rate with minimal muzzle flip. Many have looked down this barrel, but few have lived to tell of it. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum.
    .suffix = armadura-piercing
ent-WeaponRevolverPirate = pirate revólver
    .desc = A crude single-action revolver handmade by a space pirate. Old and covered in rust, it somehow still works. Loads 5 rounds of .45 magnum.
ent-WeaponRevolverPirateEmpty = pirate revólver
    .desc = A crude single-action revolver handmade by a space pirate. Old and covered in rust, it somehow still works. Loads 5 rounds of .45 magnum.
    .suffix = Empty
ent-WeaponRevolverPython = python
    .desc = A powerful double-action revolver manufactured by the Syndicate. Loud and flashy, perfect for any agent looking to make a statement. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum. Can be double-shot burst fired to really bring the pain.
ent-WeaponRevolverPythonAP = python
    .desc = A powerful double-action revolver manufactured by the Syndicate. Loud and flashy, perfect for any agent looking to make a statement. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum. Can be double-shot burst fired to really bring the pain.
    .suffix = armadura-piercing
ent-WeaponRevolverZOZ = TOZ-82 'Jupiter'
    .desc = An oversized bullpup revolver whose design was smuggled out of the USSP. You might need both hands for this one. It's got a flip-out bayonet, but the damned thing is stuck shut. Loads 6 rounds of .45 magnum.
